{"text": "All caps on a school website. Looks like a detail. Now multiply it by a thousand schools.\n\nEvery school has the same duties: accessibility, data protection, security, and rules that keep changing. Most face them alone, with their own budget and their own contractor. So quality comes down to chance.\n\nCleverphant is shared digital infrastructure for schools. What people see is the website. Underneath is what keeps it right: compliance, training, support, and a network that connects every school.\n\nBecause every school runs on the same system, they all get the same benefits, and the same bugs. But it takes just one school to notice. Fixed once, fixed for all.\n\nIdeas travel the same way. A curious school leader brings a need. Their school becomes the pilot. When the data shows it works, it becomes the standard for every school.\n\nAnd it works from the top, too. A municipality or a ministry publishes a new rule or a campaign once, and it appears on every school website at the same time.\n\nA small village school gets what a large city school gets. A family changing schools finds a familiar place. The foundation is shared; the face stays the school's own. Not identical. Equally good.\n\nChange starts with details. Being small is no excuse to look away. Stop writing in capitals, stop stretching text, stop hiding information in images, get cookie consent right. That's our Trojan elephant, in the good sense. Once it works everywhere, we go further: a document bank, whistleblower protection, bookings, and next, AI integrations. Because AI can't work in chaos.\n\nWhat works in one school works in a municipality, a region, a whole country. Schools can be added quickly, while costs grow far more slowly. Not a promise of cheap. The logic of scale.\n\nWe have walked this road for fifteen years. Hundreds of institutions, whole municipalities on one standard, with content audits, proven onboarding and a training platform. Built in a small country. Ready for yours. 